        <mxCell id="note_box" value="" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#666666;dashed=1;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="905" width="980" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="note_text" value="&lt;b&gt;Real Tcl &amp;quot;expect&amp;quot; semantics:&lt;/b&gt; patterns are matched against whatever text next appears in the SSH buffer, not evaluated as a strict if/elif chain -- but when a single output block contains text matching more than one pattern (e.g. an error message containing both &amp;quot;exceeds platform capacity&amp;quot; and the word &amp;quot;error&amp;quot;), the pattern listed earlier in source (src/exp/myexpect.exp) wins, per the priority test documented in DEVELOPMENT.md. &amp;quot;Object doesn&amp;#39;t exist&amp;quot; is the one non-fatal branch: exp_continue re-arms the same expect and keeps waiting on the same buffer instead of exiting -- see TROUBLESHOOTING.md &amp;quot;Object doesn&amp;#39;t exist&amp;quot; and ts-agent-lifecycle.drawio.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Callers&lt;/b&gt; (each sources myexpect.exp): ssh-init.exp &amp;bull; tsagent-configured.exp &amp;bull; tsagent-modify-panorama.exp &amp;bull; tsagent-modify-firewall.exp &amp;bull; tsagent-not-connected.exp &amp;mdash; see ssh-session-lifecycle.drawio for the login sequence that first establishes the session this decision tree then guards." style="text;html=1;fontSize=10;align=left;whiteSpace=wrap;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="80" y="915" width="940" height="110" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
